build: find libyaml without its pkg-config file

The saved icon positions are YAML, read and written with libyaml, which
meson looks up as the pkg-config module yaml-0.1. Only libyaml's Autotools
build installs yaml-0.1.pc; a libyaml built with its CMake files (as the
one in this tree is) installs the library, yaml.h and CMake package files,
and no .pc. Fall back to looking for the library and its header, so file
icons are not silently built out (or the configuration refused) because of
the missing metadata.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -61,7 +61,11 @@
 gtk_layer_shell = dependency('gtk-layer-shell-0', version: dependency_versions['gtk-layer-shell'], required: get_option('wayland'))
 
 # Feature file-icons
-libyaml = dependency('yaml-0.1', version: dependency_versions['libyaml'], required: get_option('desktop-icons') and get_option('file-icons'))
+libyaml = dependency('yaml-0.1', version: dependency_versions['libyaml'], required: false)
+if not libyaml.found()
+  # libyaml built with its CMake files installs no yaml-0.1.pc
+  libyaml = cc.find_library('yaml', has_headers: 'yaml.h', required: get_option('desktop-icons') and get_option('file-icons'))
+endif
 
 feature_cflags = []
 
